---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---
<Layout
  title="terms of service"
  description="The terms of service for using the adore Discord bot and website."
>
  <Prose heading="Terms of service" updated="August 2026">
    <p>
      By adding or using <strong>{site.name}</strong> (the "bot") or this website,
      you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the bot.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not use the bot to break Discord's Terms of Service or Community Guidelines.</li>
      <li>Do not abuse, overload, or attempt to disrupt the bot or its infrastructure.</li>
      <li>Do not use the bot for harassment, illegal activity, or distributing harmful content.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Availability</h2>
    <p>
      The bot is provided "as is" and "as available". We may modify, suspend, or
      discontinue features at any time without notice. We do not guarantee
      uninterrupted or error-free operation.
    </p>

    <h2>Premium &amp; payments</h2>
    <p>
      Premium and Private Instance features may be offered for
      a fee. Payments are processed by third-party providers. Open a ticket in
      the support server to purchase or transfer a subscription. See our
      <a href="/premium">premium page</a> and <a href="/refunds">refund policy</a> for details.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect,
      incidental, or consequential damages arising from use of the bot.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms? Reach us in the
      <a href={site.support} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">support server</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
